  "status": "Approved",
  "description": "The proposal involves replacing the existing gravel surface to the hotel's car-park area with a permeable paving system. ",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the end of three years from the date of this permission.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to comply with the provisions of Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).\r\n\r\n",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\n\r\n2025-5503-001 Rev.A; 2025-5503-TR01 (1); Document titled 'CellWeb TRP Tree Root Protection Guaranteed' prepared by Geosynthetics; Flood Risk Assessment and Drainage Strategy ref. 128KT-FRA-01 dated January 2026 prepared by Arbtech; 128KH - P-01; TCP01 Rev.01; TPP01 Rev.01; 45022009_TS01; Arboricultural Method Statement ref. 45022009_AMS01 dated 31 March 2026 prepared by Arbtech; 128KH - P-00; Design Access Statement prepared by Adara; AIA01 Rev.01.\r\n\r\nReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interest of proper planning.\r\n",
    "Condition : 3 - All new external work shall be carried out in materials that resemble, as closely as possible, in colour and texture those of the existing building, unless otherwise specified in the approved application. \r\n\r\nReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area in accordance with the requirements of policy D1 of the London Borough of Camden Local Plan 2017. \r\n",
    "Condition : 4 - Prior to the commencement of works on site, tree protection measures shall be installed and working practices adopted in accordance with the document entitled \"Arboricultural Method Statement\" dated 31 March 2026 by Arbtech ref. 45022009_AMS01 and \"Tree Protection Plan\" dated March 2026 by Arbtech ref. TPP01 Rev.01.  All trees on the site, or parts of trees grow from adjoining sites, unless shown on the permitted drawings as being removed, shall be retained and protected from damage in accordance with BS5837:2012 and with the approved protection details. The development shall be monitored by the project arboriculturalist in accordance with the approved report.\r\n\r\nReason: To ensure that the development will not have an adverse effect on existing trees and in order to maintain the character and amenity of the area in accordance with the requirements of policies A2 and A3 of the Camden Local Plan 2017. \r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - Prior to commencement of development, full details in respect of the following shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority: \r\n\r\na)\tMaintenance schedule for the proposed components of the paving system;\r\nb)\tAdditional commentary on how the proposed SuDS measure has considered the reduction of blockages to ensure proposed system is viable; and\r\nc)\tAdditional commentary and/or diagram to demonstrate in the event of a design exceedance, how have the design / topography factored in exceedance flow to prevent ingress of water into the building and to neighbouring areas. \r\n\r\nReason: To reduce the rate of surface water run-off from the development and limit the impact on the storm-water drainage system in accordance with policies CC2 and CC3 of the London Borough of Camden Local Plan 2017.\r\n"
  ],
